; print --forecast lists only the months whose running total passes the
; predicate, so print must compute the running total when --forecast is
; given.
;
; print shows no running total, so to save its cost calc_posts computes
; one for print only when an option can read it.  The --forecast
; (--forecast-while) predicate can: besides deciding when forecast_posts
; stops, it filters every posting after calc_posts, just before the
; output.  Without the running total the filter would see each forecast
; posting's own amount, $-100, which always passes, and print would list
; every month up to the five-year forecast limit: 61 transactions instead
; of 9.  So --forecast turns the running total on by its presence alone,
; whatever the predicate calls the total (`T`, `total`, `O`).
;
; Each periodic posting is forecast in a transaction of its own, and the
; query keeps the Assets:Checking ones.  print passes on every posting of
; a matching transaction, so Opening adds $250 and $-250 and the total is
; $0 when the forecast begins.  The forecast starts with the current
; month, January 2024, and lowers the total by $100 a month; in the tenth
; month, October 2024, the total reaches $-1000, which fails the
; predicate, so nine forecast transactions are printed, January to
; September 2024.  print holds postings back until the forecast is
; complete, so it is this filter, not forecast_posts, that ends the list.
; Without --generated, print leaves out the generated postings and shows
; only their transactions' headers; the second test shows them, and
; spells the option and the total out in full.

~ monthly
    Assets:Checking   $-100
    Expenses:Rent

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Checking   $250
    Equity:Opening

test print --now 2024/01/15 --forecast 'T>{$-1000.00}' Assets:Checking
2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Checking                             $250
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/01 Forecast transaction

2024/02/01 Forecast transaction

2024/03/01 Forecast transaction

2024/04/01 Forecast transaction

2024/05/01 Forecast transaction

2024/06/01 Forecast transaction

2024/07/01 Forecast transaction

2024/08/01 Forecast transaction

2024/09/01 Forecast transaction
end test

test print --now 2024/01/15 --generated --forecast-while 'total>{$-1000.00}' Assets:Checking
2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Checking                             $250
    Equity:Opening                             $-250

2024/01/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/02/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/03/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/04/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/05/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/06/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/07/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/08/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100

2024/09/01 Forecast transaction
    Assets:Checking                            $-100
end test

; select ... from xacts prints through print's printer, but without
; print's --related-all nothing holds the postings back: each forecast
; posting reaches the running total as it is generated, and only those
; matching the where clause count.  The total starts at Opening's $250 in
; Assets:Checking and drops by $100 a month: December 2024 leaves $-950,
; and January 2025 would leave $-1050, which fails the predicate, so the
; forecast stops after twelve transactions.  Without the running total
; the predicate would see each posting's own $-100, and the forecast
; would run to the five-year limit again: 61 transactions.

test select payee from xacts where account =~ /Assets:Checking/ --now 2024/01/15 --forecast 'T>{$-1000.00}'
2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Checking                             $250
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/01 Forecast transaction

2024/02/01 Forecast transaction

2024/03/01 Forecast transaction

2024/04/01 Forecast transaction

2024/05/01 Forecast transaction

2024/06/01 Forecast transaction

2024/07/01 Forecast transaction

2024/08/01 Forecast transaction

2024/09/01 Forecast transaction

2024/10/01 Forecast transaction

2024/11/01 Forecast transaction

2024/12/01 Forecast transaction
end test
